# Cloudflare Pages response headers for web.joinrift.app.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# Ask every time. Flutter's files carry no version in their names, so a
# browser holding one after a deploy runs a new index.html beside an old
# main.dart.js. An unchanged file still answers 304 from its ETag.
#
# On web.joinrift.app this header is not enough by itself: the joinrift.app
# zone's Browser Cache TTL replaces it with four hours on anything that looks
# static (.js, .wasm). A response-header Transform Rule on the zone sets
# no-cache again for that host; this file covers the pages.dev addresses.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
